          ],
          "content": "Ganita Manjari | Grade 9 | Part I"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.108,
            0.887,
            0.204
          ],
          "content": "When x = 0, y = 1, so (0, 1) is a point on the line. We can call this point A. We say that the x-coordinate of A is 0 and the y-coordinate is 1. Also, when x = 3, y = 7. Thus, B (3, 7) is another point on the line. We plot these points on the coordinate plane, join them and extend the line in both directions as shown in Fig. 2.5."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.247,
            0.209,
            0.751,
            0.515
          ],
          "content": "",
